  "caption": "False-alarm count versus sensitivity for all 32 candidate readouts on the specificity panel (15 constructed no-op pairs; 9 effective pairs, or 8 for readouts that could not be evaluated on all 9). Each marker is one cell of the grid -- 32 readouts fall into 23 distinct cells -- and a marker's area and inset digit give how many readouts share it, so no readout is hidden under another. Colour and shape give the readout class. Every activation readout sits at 0-3 false alarms but none exceeds 6/9 sensitivity; the logit baselines BL1 scatter at 5-8 false alarms, and the weight-space cosine B7/B7_nullproj are the worst at 9/15 even though B7 has the highest sensitivity of any activation or weight readout (7/9). The single most sensitive readout is the text-only greedy_refusal_rate (7/8) at 2 false alarms. No readout reaches both zero false alarms and high sensitivity: the best zero-false-alarm readout is text-only greedy_refusal_rate_onset at 5/8, and the best zero-false-alarm activation readout is N6 at 5/9. Markers are dodged horizontally by class by at most 0.12 so coincident readouts of different classes stay visible; the dashed line at 4 marks the band no readout occupies. AMS_T2_drift (0/8) later failed validation against the reproduced pair list, and the two regex readouts were flagged unverifiable; all three are plotted as recorded in aggregates.json.",
  "legend": {
    "loc": "lower right",
    "fontsize": 9,
    "title": "Marker area = readouts in cell"
  }
